@tracking = https://localhost:7059
@merchant = merchant-1

### 1. Create a shipment
POST {{tracking}}/merchants/{{merchant}}/shipments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "merchantReference": "ORDER-1001",
  "carrier": "FastShip",
  "trackingNumber": "FS123456",
  "promisedBy": "2026-10-25T18:00:00+02:00"
}

### 2. "Delivered" arrives first
POST {{tracking}}/carrier-events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "carrier": "FastShip",
  "trackingNumber": "FS123456",
  "carrierEventId": "fs-3",
  "status": "Delivered",
  "occurredAt": "2026-10-24T14:10:00+02:00",
  "location": "Copenhagen"
}

### 3. "Out for delivery" arrives later, but happened earlier
POST {{tracking}}/carrier-events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "carrier": "FastShip",
  "trackingNumber": "FS123456",
  "carrierEventId": "fs-2",
  "status": "OutForDelivery",
  "occurredAt": "2026-10-24T08:30:00+02:00",
  "location": "Copenhagen depot"
}

### 4. The carrier sends the same event again
POST {{tracking}}/carrier-events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "carrier": "FastShip",
  "trackingNumber": "FS123456",
  "carrierEventId": "fs-2",
  "status": "OutForDelivery",
  "occurredAt": "2026-10-24T08:30:00+02:00",
  "location": "Copenhagen depot"
}

### 5. Read it back
GET {{tracking}}/merchants/{{merchant}}/shipments?reference=ORDER-1001

### 6. Another merchant sees nothing
GET {{tracking}}/merchants/merchant-2/shipments?reference=ORDER-1001

### 7. Retry the create: same shipment, no duplicate
POST {{tracking}}/merchants/{{merchant}}/shipments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "merchantReference": "ORDER-1001",
  "carrier": "FastShip",
  "trackingNumber": "FS123456",
  "promisedBy": "2026-10-25T18:00:00+02:00"
}

### Active FastShip shipments (should be [])
GET {{tracking}}/carriers/fastship/active-shipments

### Active NordPost shipments (should be [])
GET {{tracking}}/carriers/nordpost/active-shipments